<DocsLayout title="Chudware documentation" description="Install Chudware, build your first part, and move from sketch to manufacturing with practical, task-focused guides." section="Start here">
  <h2>Build something real</h2>
  <p>These guides follow the shape of an engineering project: install the desktop app, create constrained geometry, assemble parts, prepare manufacturing work, and keep the project traceable.</p>
  <p>If this is your first session, begin with <a href="/docs/install-windows/">installation</a> for your platform, then continue to <a href="/docs/first-part/">your first part</a>.</p>
  <h2>Use the copilot as a collaborator</h2>
  <p>The AI copilot can inspect and change the open design, but it does not replace engineering judgment. Review the feature tree, measurements, and highlighted changes before accepting the result.</p>
  <h2>Keep help close</h2>
  <p>Use the documentation menu to move between guides. Search runs entirely in your browser against a static index shipped with this site; your query is not sent to a search provider.</p>
</DocsLayout>
